.Dd December 21, 2026
.Dt ICOWM-MEMGUARD 5
.Os icowm-1.0.1
.Sh NAME
.Nm memguard.json
.Nd restricted-memory configuration for IcoWM
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Pa memguard.json
is read only when
.Xr icowm 1
is started with
.Fl M Ar mib .
An ordinary session never looks at it, and it has no effect at all
without that option.
.Pp
For that one session it replaces
.Pa config.json
entirely, which is not consulted at all.
.Pa bindings.json
and a theme under
.Pa themes/
are still read exactly as usual.
The file is optional: missing or unreadable, a fixed built-in profile is
used instead.
.Pp
Only the keys below are ever read; anything else in the file is
silently ignored.
Each has the same meaning as the key of the same name in
.Xr icowm 5 ,
so only the differences are spelled out here.
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Ic theme
.It Ic programs.editor
.It Ic programs.file-manager
.It Ic programs.launcher
.It Ic programs.terminal
.It Ic programs.web-browser
.It Ic desktops.margins.top
.It Ic desktops.margins.right
.It Ic desktops.margins.bottom
.It Ic desktops.margins.left
.It Ic windows.move-step
.It Ic windows.show-geom
.It Ic windows.gravity
.It Ic windows.edges.snap.window
.It Ic windows.edges.snap.screen
.It Ic windows.edges.resistance
.It Ic windows.focus.policy
.It Ic windows.focus.focus-new
.It Ic windows.focus.raise
.It Ic windows.placement.policy
.It Ic windows.placement.monitor
.It Ic windows.placement.group-related
.It Ic icons.show-geom
.It Ic icons.placement.policy
.It Ic systray
.It Ic shutdown.enable-emergency-shortcut
.It Ic shutdown.timeout-seconds
As in
.Xr icowm 5 .
.It Ic prompt.is-enabled Pq boolean, default Ql true
As in
.Xr icowm 5 ,
except that this mode defaults it to true rather than false,
deliberately, so that the launcher binding opens the built-in box rather
than spawning a separate process.
.El
.Ss What this mode fixes regardless of the file
The screen count, the desktop count, the RandR handling and the
startup-notification setting are fixed in this mode and cannot be
configured here at all.
The single desktop the session starts with stays the only one: the
window list's entries for adding and removing a desktop, and their
bindings, do not appear at all rather than appearing and refusing.
.Pp
Three more are read and then overridden, since this mode never docks a
tray icon:
.Ic systray.text.position
and
.Ic systray.order
are forced back to
.Ql left
and
.Ql left-to-right ,
and embedding itself can never be switched on.
The tray still shows its clock, battery and frame while
.Ic systray.is-enabled
is true; it simply accepts no docked application icon.
.Pp
.Ic windows.solid-drag
is different again: it is not accepted in the file at all, rather than
read and overridden, since this mode always runs with it off.
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Pa ${XDG_CONFIG_HOME}/icowm/memguard.json
The file this page describes, at the first of the several locations
.Xr icowm 1
looks in.
.El
.Sh EXAMPLES
A profile for a small machine, keeping the launcher in-process and the
tray to its clock alone:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
{
    "programs": { "terminal": "xterm -fn fixed" },
    "prompt": { "is-enabled": true },
    "windows": {
        "focus": { "policy": "sloppy" },
        "placement": { "policy": "cascade" }
    },
    "systray": {
        "is-enabled": true,
        "clock": { "is-enabled": true, "format": "%R" },
        "battery": { "is-enabled": true }
    }
}
.Ed
.Pp
Start a session with a ceiling of 24 mebibytes, which is what makes this
file be read at all:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
exec icowm -M 24
.Ed
